Okay.

765
00:39:21,826 --> 00:39:23,326
Okay.

766
00:39:25,129 --> 00:39:28,810
Okay, let's see if I can
imagine the whole thing.

767
00:39:28,834 --> 00:39:31,079
Objection! Speculation.

768
00:39:31,103 --> 00:39:33,981
Your Honor, I
just said "imagine."

769
00:39:34,005 --> 00:39:37,985
If speculation, uh,
pleases everyone,

770
00:39:38,009 --> 00:39:39,620
may I speculate?

771
00:39:39,644 --> 00:39:41,089
Will it get us anywhere?

772
00:39:41,113 --> 00:39:43,858
Oh, I believe it will. I
think... I know it will.

773
00:39:43,882 --> 00:39:47,128
Very well, then.
Proceed, Mr. Matlock.

774
00:39:47,152 --> 00:39:48,917
Thank you.

775
00:39:50,721 --> 00:39:56,337
Mr. Ullman was a pretty
obsessive person, wasn't he?

776
00:39:56,361 --> 00:39:59,607
He always wanted
everything in the right place.

777
00:39:59,631 --> 00:40:01,175
When things weren't
in the right place,

778
00:40:01,199 --> 00:40:02,443
he'd have a fit, wouldn't he?

779
00:40:02,467 --> 00:40:04,044
I guess so.

780
00:40:04,068 --> 00:40:06,614
And that particular
day, what with the...

781
00:40:06,638 --> 00:40:10,050
The, uh, unpleasant
meeting with, uh,

782
00:40:10,074 --> 00:40:12,386
Mr. Ridgely and Miss Barnes

783
00:40:12,410 --> 00:40:15,322
and my client creating
that ruckus, you...

784
00:40:15,346 --> 00:40:17,791
You tried especially
hard to have everything

785
00:40:17,815 --> 00:40:19,493
just in its right
place, didn't you?

786
00:40:19,517 --> 00:40:21,895
As I always did.

787
00:40:21,919 --> 00:40:23,731
Imagine your surprise

788
00:40:23,755 --> 00:40:27,702
<i>when he walked out
of his dressing room</i>

789
00:40:27,726 --> 00:40:31,806
<i>onto the stage and you looked</i>

790
00:40:31,830 --> 00:40:33,474
<i>and saw the creams</i>

791
00:40:33,498 --> 00:40:35,943
<i>that you had just checked</i>

792
00:40:35,967 --> 00:40:37,345
<i>a few minutes before</i>

793
00:40:37,369 --> 00:40:38,645
<i>were in the wrong place.</i>

794
00:40:38,669 --> 00:40:42,583
<i>You switched 'em back. Whew!</i>

795
00:40:42,607 --> 00:40:45,308
<i>Then you forgot about it...</i>

796
00:40:47,612 --> 00:40:50,792
till Mr. Ullman died,

797
00:40:50,816 --> 00:40:55,796
and then you put it
all together, didn't you?

798
00:40:55,820 --> 00:41:01,201
You knew that he would
never drink regular tea...

799
00:41:01,225 --> 00:41:06,540
Didn't drink... regular tea.

800
00:41:06,564 --> 00:41:09,944
So he wasn't poisoned that way.

801
00:41:09,968 --> 00:41:14,448
You figured out that
during those few minutes

802
00:41:14,472 --> 00:41:15,682
you were in his dressing room

803
00:41:15,706 --> 00:41:17,551
taking care of that
little disturbance

804
00:41:17,575 --> 00:41:21,755
created by my client,

805
00:41:21,779 --> 00:41:25,192
someone used that opportunity

806
00:41:25,216 --> 00:41:30,164
to slip under the
stage, over to the box,

807
00:41:30,188 --> 00:41:34,801
and substitute poisoned cream

808
00:41:34,825 --> 00:41:37,772
for the regular cream.

809
00:41:37,796 --> 00:41:40,908
I... And then you
knew that same person,

810
00:41:40,932 --> 00:41:45,345
after Mr. Ullman
started his show,

811
00:41:45,369 --> 00:41:48,649
slipped into his dressing room

812
00:41:48,673 --> 00:41:51,552
with a teapot full of poison

813
00:41:51,576 --> 00:41:53,521
to implicate my client,

814
00:41:53,545 --> 00:41:55,823
and you decided
to try out your theory

815
00:41:55,847 --> 00:42:02,930
on the three people
who would benefit most

816
00:42:02,954 --> 00:42:07,134
and who were all
present that day:

817
00:42:07,158 --> 00:42:12,795
Stephen Spector, Jane
Barnes, Don Ridgely.

818
00:42:15,633 --> 00:42:20,046
And you promised not to go to
the police with what you knew,

819
00:42:20,070 --> 00:42:23,250
and one of them

820
00:42:23,274 --> 00:42:26,086
gave you that case full of...

821
00:42:26,110 --> 00:42:28,656
What was it?
Fifty-thousand, $100,000?

822
00:42:28,680 --> 00:42:30,358
No, now, none of that is true.

823
00:42:30,382 --> 00:42:35,496
Mr. Pritchard, if I were you,

824
00:42:35,520 --> 00:42:38,666
I would hope that
everyone believes

825
00:42:38,690 --> 00:42:46,690
that that's true,
because if it isn't,

826
00:42:47,164 --> 00:42:49,176
there's only one thing left.

827
00:42:51,069 --> 00:42:52,880
You were the only one

828
00:42:52,904 --> 00:42:58,474
who knew the poison
was in that cream.

829
00:42:59,877 --> 00:43:01,155
So therefore,

830
00:43:01,179 --> 00:43:06,727
you must have
killed Robert Ullman.

831
00:43:06,751 --> 00:43:09,830
I didn't kill anybody.

832
00:43:12,290 --> 00:43:16,837
Perhaps you'd like to
reconsider your testimony,

833
00:43:16,861 --> 00:43:19,440
and tell us who did.

834
00:43:29,908 --> 00:43:33,676
<i>Mr. Pritchard... we're waiting.</i>

835
00:43:33,745 --> 00:43:35,812
If one of those three people

836
00:43:35,881 --> 00:43:39,482
didn't kill Robert
Ullman, then you did.

837
00:43:39,551 --> 00:43:42,952
Now, I don't think you did.

838
00:43:43,021 --> 00:43:44,420
Blackmail is one thing,

839
00:43:44,489 --> 00:43:47,824
but murder is
another altogether.

840
00:43:47,893 --> 00:43:53,396
But the arrow is...
pointing at you.

841
00:43:53,464 --> 00:43:55,464
Look into your mind.

842
00:43:57,702 --> 00:43:59,903
One of those three

843
00:43:59,971 --> 00:44:03,907
brought that
briefcase full of money

844
00:44:03,975 --> 00:44:09,245
to a place you had prearranged,

845
00:44:09,313 --> 00:44:15,451
and there, made the exchange
that bought your silence...

846
00:44:16,855 --> 00:44:19,155
<i>until now.</i>

847
00:44:19,223 --> 00:44:21,057
<i>We are ready, Mr. Pritchard.</i>

848
00:44:21,125 --> 00:44:23,860
<i>Let us look into your mind.</i>

849
00:44:23,929 --> 00:44:27,396
<i>Let us see your memory.</i>

850
00:44:27,465 --> 00:44:33,235
<i>Who is that person,
Mr. Pritchard?</i>

851
00:44:33,304 --> 00:44:35,772
<i>Who did it?</i>

852
00:44:35,840 --> 00:44:39,809
<i>Who killed Robert Ullman?</i>

853
00:44:42,981 --> 00:44:46,515
<i>Jane Barnes.</i>

854
00:44:53,424 --> 00:44:55,269
No further questions,
Your Honor.

855
00:44:55,293 --> 00:44:57,171
Does the state wish to speak?

856
00:44:57,195 --> 00:44:58,561
Yes.

857
00:44:58,630 --> 00:45:00,470
Your Honor, in light of
these new developments,

858
00:45:00,531 --> 00:45:03,032
we would like to entertain
a motion for dismissal.

859
00:45:03,101 --> 00:45:04,634
Bailiff. Motion granted.

860
00:45:04,703 --> 00:45:06,681
Case is dismissed.
Court is adjourned.

861
00:45:07,973 --> 00:45:11,674
Mr. Matlock, I don't
know how to thank you.

862
00:45:11,743 --> 00:45:13,454
Oh, this is Alice
Wierman, my fiancee.

863
00:45:13,478 --> 00:45:15,022
Oh, hello. Hello.

864
00:45:15,046 --> 00:45:16,913
Good to see you.
Oh, nice to meet you.

865
00:45:16,982 --> 00:45:19,582
Thank you so much for
everything you've done for Hal.

866
00:45:19,651 --> 00:45:21,350
Alice has agreed
to take me back.

867
00:45:21,419 --> 00:45:24,887
Oh, well, here's a
wedding present.

868
00:45:24,956 --> 00:45:26,300
But that's your payment.

869
00:45:26,324 --> 00:45:29,058
Oh, I know, but a
priceless heirloom...

870
00:45:29,127 --> 00:45:31,694
My conscience
would never permit it.

871
00:45:31,763 --> 00:45:34,041
Thank you,
Mr. Matlock. Thank you.

872
00:45:34,065 --> 00:45:35,375
Thank you. Thank you.

873
00:45:35,399 --> 00:45:37,959
Bye-bye. Bye.

874
00:45:38,469 --> 00:45:42,471
Well, ya... ya just blew $75.

875
00:45:42,540 --> 00:45:44,173
Yeah.

876
00:45:44,242 --> 00:45:46,575
Want to spring for a hot dog?

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
